  - Custom object tracking: trackOriginalFieldConfigCustom() (line 1103) — Preserves originally-present custom objects
  - Custom preservation: Lines 667-671 ensure custom object isn't dropped if it was originally present

  Migration Orchestration

  /Users/asridhar/work/Sourcegraph/code/cmp/grafana/apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/migrate.go — Coordinates the migration pipeline
  - Tracking phase: Line 129 — trackOriginalFieldConfigCustom() marks panels that had fieldConfig.defaults.custom before migrations
  - Migration execution: Lines 177-185 — Runs v38 and other migrations
  - Cleanup phase: Line 193 — cleanupDashboardForSave() applies final cleanup

  The Bug

  The issue appears to be in v38.go, processPanelsV38() (lines 116-127): The code only processes defaults.custom if a displayMode property exists. If a table panel's custom object has other properties but no
  displayMode, or if custom exists but is empty, the migration may not preserve it properly. Additionally, the cleanup phase in cleanupFieldConfigDefaults() may remove empty custom objects for table panels
  when they should be preserved.
